work so I don't=20
> > know how to get the ddf (although 1st I have to figure out the g(y).=20
> >  =20
I really have know idea what you are saying here.  It sounds like you=20
are saying that your transects were opportunistic or were haphazard (no=20
sampling plan).  That is different than saying they are not systematic. =20
Systematic and random have specific meanings.  If I'm correct then what=20
you need is to use some of the spatial modeling capability which I=20
believe is coming in a future version of DISTANCE but I don't know it's=20
status.  I have written an R package called DSpat but it is also not=20
ready for distribution at this point in time.

regards --jeff

