Ana-

Yes you can get them with MRDS as you noted. The probabilities are=20
computed and stored in the R object. If they are in MCDS I don't know=20
whether they can be output or not. I didn't write MCDS and Len will have=20
to answer that for you. Also, the error message you are getting is=20
coming from the Distance interface and not from the R mrds package, so=20
Len will also have to help you with that one. You always have the option=20
of using the R mrds package directly with R. One consideration for Lucia=20
is that mrds does not yet (I think) allow adjustment functions to the=20
key like mcds. So if that is important you may want to stick with mcds=20
and figure out a way to compute the p's. Again Len is the best person to=20
address the status of adding adjustment functions to mrds.

regards --jeff

